      "problem": "A laboratory beaker has a volume of $1$ cup. What is this volume in fluid ounces?",
      "worked_solution": "A table showing the customary units of volume is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Gallon | $\\text{gal}$ | $1\\,\\text{gal}=8\\,\\text{pints}$ |\n| Pint | $\\text{pt}$ | $1\\,\\text{pt}=2\\,\\text{cups}$ |\n| Cup | $-$ | $1\\,\\text{cup}=8\\,\\text{fl oz}$ |\n| Fluid ounce | $\\text{fl oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\text{cup}$ is equivalent to $8\\,\\text{fluid ounces}.$",
